            "id": "H002",
            "statement": "The field K has characteristic p.",
            "origin": "problem.md:16"
          },
          {
            "id": "H003",
            "statement": "0 <= lambda < p.",
            "origin": "problem.md:17"
          },
          {
            "id": "H004",
            "statement": "With the representation act, V=V(lambda) is the complex irreducible highest-weight sl2(C)-module of highest weight lambda and has complex dimension lambda+1.",
            "origin": "problem.md:18-20"
          },
          {
            "id": "H005",
            "statement": "L=sl2(C), and x,y,h are its Chevalley generators, satisfying [h,x]=2x, [h,y]=-2y and [x,y]=h.",
            "origin": "problem.md:18-24"
          },
          {
            "id": "H006",
            "statement": "v is nonzero, xv=0, and hv=lambda v.",
            "origin": "problem.md:26-27"
          },
          {
            "id": "H007",
            "statement": "M is an admissible lattice in V: it is a free abelian subgroup possessing an integer basis which is also a complex basis of V, and is stable under U_Z. M is arbitrary and is not assumed to be the minimal lattice.",
            "origin": "problem.md:30-32"
          }
        ],
        "conclusion": "V_K is nonzero, and for every K-linear subspace W of V_K, if W is invariant under x_K,y_K,h_K (the action rho of the Chevalley generators of L_K), then W={0} or W=V_K. Thus V(K) is irreducible as an L(K)-module."
